{
 "_note": "Kindergarten \"How Books and Print Work\" (English literacy year, Part 12.3; types/_shared/print-concepts-k.js). THE TEACHER READS every instruction, title and sentence; a child points, dots, circles, colors, cuts and glues, writes a number or a page number, and traces or copies a short title or sentence. `pics`: the library picture of a word (colour themes only, each looked at) and its kind (two pictures of one kind never share a page). `books`: invented books (title, author, the cover picture, the first sentence of the story and its picture); `famous`: titles a class may know (no title of the bank shares two content words or its first two words with one). `makeTitles`: two-word titles to copy (K-666). `twoLine`: sentences printed over two lines (\"|\" breaks the line; K-667). `frames` and `sets`: the pattern books of K-668 ({n} is a pictured thing; `anWords` take \"an\" and stand only after \"the\"). `dots`: the sentences of K-669 by level, with a picture; `look*`: the words, letters and numbers of \"Circle the word\"; `confusable`: a letter and a digit a child can take for one another (never in one row). `lengths`: words by first letter in three lengths (S one syllable and at most four letters, M two syllables and five to seven letters, L three syllables or more and eight letters or more; K-670): any two words of neighbouring lengths of one letter differ by a printed width of 1.35 times or more and by two letters (S to M) or three (M to L); `lengthPics`: the ones whose picture a child names with exactly that word; `neverRow`: pairs that never share a row; `pairs`: a picture and two sentences that start alike (K-670 level 3). `count`: the sentences of K-671 by level; `syl`: syllables of the sentence words; `sylMore`: words some speakers say with one beat more (a sentence holds its rule for every pronunciation). `spaces`: the sentences of K-672 (read: with and without spaces; cards1, cards2, cards3: three, four and five words to cut and glue; copy: three words to copy). `banned`: words no page prints.",
